    "body": "Maintainer decision (question dialog, 2026-11-25): #3616 and #3622 are part of this issue now. Their pins move here.\n\nFrom #3616:\n- When the HSM plan of a planar level falls back to rings (`machining3d/hsm.rs`, `plan_level`), plan the rings with the start side of the level.\n- Keep Auto byte-identical.\n- Add a pin that reaches the fallback with Inside and Outside.\n- This can change posted moves. Thus it is under the safety floor.\n\nFrom #3622:\n- The number in the `StrategyFallback` warning is the number of areas (or levels, by a stated word) that fell back.\n- Add a pin for two levels with the same uncut area.\n- Add a pin for the Adaptive ring fallback with a guard fallback.\n- The paths are `pocket_avoid.rs:158-159` and `pocket_hsm.rs:85-95`.\n\nThe moved code of this issue keeps its output. These two fixes change behaviour, so name them in the PR.\n",
